Hi Ajay,

Graham has limited computer access at the moment to the internet, and I am expecting my first baby any day now.

I have had this issue before, and I am trying to remember the fix for it.

I believe that you may have a corrupted Rdata file in your working directory / folder.

If you set your working directory to a new one, or you clear out the rattle rdata files from your current working directory, I think should fix the problem.

To find your working directory, go to the R console and type
getwd()

to change your working directory you type into the R concole

setwd(" ..........")

insert into the ...........  your operating system specific syntax

er got windows it would be

setwd("c:/a")

Hope this works
Regards
Tony

